Forward physical window activation and service the original message wait.

The unchanged original capture observes WM_ACTIVATEAPP at 0x4132f0,
its inactive return at 0x41344d (activation/stored timer zero, held key retained),
and WaitMessage at 0x4130a3. The first independent startup callback survives
cancellation of the stored second timer. Message wakes can advance the menu
while inactive: waiting until reactivation alone changes the original flow.

Enter the registered procedure for actual platform focus transitions, dedupe
activation and preserve the existing ShowWindow-before-explicit-timer order.
Interactive WaitMessage waits for new platform window/input events, yielding
with audio/CD/timer/movie services running. No engine clock return or frame
counter is synthesized. Headless replay retains its existing path. This does
not establish whole-game/physical audio timing or all OS-message fidelity.

